---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Change the record when the evidence changes." description="Material factual errors should be corrected promptly. Significant corrections should remain visible">
  <section class="shell route">
    <header class="route-head">
      <div class="kicker">/ CORRECTIONS</div>
      <h1>Change the record when the evidence changes.</h1>
    </header>
    <div style="max-width:var(--reading);font:1.18rem/1.65 var(--reader)">
      <p>Material factual errors should be corrected promptly. Significant corrections should remain visible
through the article change log rather than being hidden by silently rewriting the record.</p>
<p>These categories remain distinct:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>CORRECTION</strong> — A material factual error has been fixed. The original claim was wrong.</li>
  <li><strong>CLARIFICATION</strong> — The original was technically accurate but imprecise or misleading without additional context. No fact changed.</li>
  <li><strong>UPDATE</strong> — New information or a developing story. The original was accurate at the time of publication.</li>
  <li><strong>PRESENTATION CHANGE</strong> — Visual, structural, or formatting change with no factual impact. A chart was redrawn, a table was reformatted, or a figure was repositioned.</li>
</ul>
<p>Significant corrections remain visible in article change logs. Minor clarifications may be incorporated silently if they do not alter the meaning of any claim.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  ul {
    margin: 12px 0;
    padding-left: 20px;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  li strong {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: .88rem;
    letter-spacing: .03em;
  }
</style>
